---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageIntro from '../../components/PageIntro.astro';
import EnvironmentMap from '../../components/EnvironmentMap.astro';
import Principles from '../../components/Principles.astro';
import StatusTag from '../../components/StatusTag.astro';
import ContactCTA from '../../components/ContactCTA.astro';
import Button from '../../components/Button.astro';
import { configurable, notThis } from '../../data/environment';
---

<BaseLayout
  path="environment/"
  title="The environment"
  description="What a personal intelligence environment is: one place to configure the models, agents, tools, memory and permissions behind the AI you use — and to stay in charge of them."
>
  <PageIntro
    eyebrow="The environment"
    title="What a personal intelligence environment means."
    lead="Most people meet AI as a single app with a single model behind it. A personal intelligence environment turns that around: the capabilities come to you, and you decide how they fit together."
  />

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="short-title">
    <div class="container split">
      <div class="split__aside" data-reveal>
        <p class="label">The short version</p>
        <h2 id="short-title" class="split__title">
          An operating layer for the AI you use.
        </h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose short" data-reveal data-reveal-order="1">
        <p class="short__lead">
          Your computer has an operating system. It decides which programs run, what they can touch,
          and how you work with them. You rarely think about it — but it is the reason your machine
          feels like <em>yours</em>.
        </p>
        <p>
          A personal intelligence environment plays a similar role for AI. Instead of a separate
          assistant in every app, each with its own memory and rules, you have one environment. It
          knows which models are available, which specialist agents exist, which tools may be used,
          and what it has been allowed to remember.
        </p>
        <p>
          You talk to one interface. Behind it, work is routed to whatever is best suited — and
          every part of that arrangement is something you can see, change or switch off.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section band-tone" aria-labelledby="anatomy-title">
    <div class="container stack">
      <div class="split">
        <div class="split__aside" data-reveal>
          <p class="label">Anatomy</p>
          <h2 id="anatomy-title" class="split__title">
            The parts, and who controls them.
          </h2>
        </div>
        <p class="lead" data-reveal data-reveal-order="1">
          At the centre is you. Around you, a primary interface understands what you are asking and
          coordinates the rest. Everything beyond that is a component you choose. This is the
          direction for the public product; the private system is where it is being proven.
        </p>
      </div>
      <EnvironmentMap />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="configure-title">
    <div class="container split">
      <div class="split__aside" data-reveal>
        <p class="label">Direction</p>
        <h2 id="configure-title" class="split__title">
          What you would decide.
        </h2>
        <p class="configure__note">
          This is the shape of the product APOLLO Network is working towards. None of it is publicly
          available today, and each line is marked accordingly.
        </p>
      </div>
      <dl class="spec" data-reveal data-reveal-order="1">
        {configurable.map((item) => (
          <div class="spec__row">
            <dt class="spec__term">{item.name}</dt>
            <dd class="spec__detail">{item.decide}</dd>
            <dd class="configure__status">
              <StatusTag status="future" />
            </dd>
          </div>
        ))}
      </dl>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section band-tone" aria-labelledby="philosophy-title">
    <div class="container stack">
      <div class="split">
        <div class="split__aside" data-reveal>
          <p class="label">Philosophy</p>
          <h2 id="philosophy-title" class="split__title">
            Provider-independent. User-controlled.
          </h2>
        </div>
        <div class="prose" data-reveal data-reveal-order="1">
          <p>
            The best model today will not be the best model next year. Prices change, policies
            change, companies change direction. An environment that belongs to you should be able to
            absorb all of that without you starting over.
          </p>
          <p>
            So the environment, not any one model, is the product. Models, agents and tools are
            components — swappable, comparable and accountable to the person who owns the system.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <Principles />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="not-title">
    <div class="container stack">
      <div class="split">
        <div class="split__aside" data-reveal>
          <p class="label">To be clear</p>
          <h2 id="not-title" class="split__title">
            What it is not.
          </h2>
        </div>
        <ul class="not" role="list">
          {notThis.map((item, i) => (
            <li class="not__item" data-reveal data-reveal-order={String(i)}>
              <h3 class="not__title">{item.title}</h3>
              <p class="not__body">{item.body}</p>
            </li>
          ))}
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="next" data-reveal>
        <p class="next__text">The ideas above are being tested in a real system.</p>
        <Button href="project/" variant="primary">
          See the project
        </Button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <ContactCTA />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .short__lead {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--fs-h3);
    line-height: 1.35;
    color: var(--c-text);
  }

  .short__lead em {
    font-style: normal;
    color: var(--c-blue-bright);
  }

  .configure__note {
    max-width: 24rem;
    margin-top: var(--s-5);
    color: var(--c-text-muted);
  }

  .configure__status {
    justify-self: start;
  }

  .not {
    display: grid;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
    border-top: var(--border);
  }

  .not__item {
    padding-block: var(--s-6);
    border-bottom: var(--border);
  }

  .not__title {
    font-size: var(--fs-h3);
  }

  .not__body {
    max-width: 36rem;
    margin-top: var(--s-3);
    color: var(--c-text-muted);
  }

  .next {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: var(--s-5);
    padding: var(--s-6);
    border: var(--border-strong);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    background: linear-gradient(90deg, rgb(27 77 255 / 0.12), transparent);
  }

  .next__text {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--fs-h4);
  }
</style>
